{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-163505",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\sqrt{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[\\frac{2{y}^{7/2}}{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
